This is the default position, not a considered one: without a licence file at all,
the same terms apply by operation of copyright law, and "no licence" reads to anyone
who finds the repository as "do not touch". This file only makes that explicit.

If the project should be open source, replace this file with the licence text you
want — MIT for "do what you like, keep the notice", Apache-2.0 for the same plus an
explicit patent grant, GPL-3.0 to require that derivatives stay open. That choice is
the owner's to make, and it is much easier to make now than after other people have
started contributing under terms nobody wrote down.
